// Title: Security event log cleared (Event 1102)
// MITRE: T1070.001 (Clear Windows Event Logs) [v19: Defense Impairment]
// Data sources: SecurityEvent (Windows Security channel)
// False positive notes: Near-zero. The Security log is essentially never cleared in normal
//                       operations. A cleared log during business hours from a non-admin
//                       workstation is incident-grade. Log-management tooling that archives+clears
//                       is the only real FP - allow-list those service accounts.
// Author: detection pack maintainers
// Date: 2026-06-27
//
// The System/Security-channel corroboration for the registry audit-tamper rule (v4/04). When an
// operator clears tracks, Event 1102 is written to the very log being cleared - a self-witnessing
// artifact. Promote to P1.

SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where EventID == 1102
| extend ClearedBy = coalesce(column_ifexists("SubjectUserName", ""), Account)
| extend Phase = "DefenseImpair-LogClear"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, EventID, Activity, ClearedBy,
          SubjectDomainName = column_ifexists("SubjectDomainName", ""),
          SubjectLogonId = column_ifexists("SubjectLogonId", ""), Phase
| order by TimeGenerated desc
